 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "Archimedes once claimed he could move the whole Earth.",
   "s": 0.151,
   "e": 2.741
  },
  {
   "text": "So the king said:",
   "s": 3.157,
   "e": 4.031
  },
  {
   "text": "prove it.",
   "s": 4.232,
   "e": 4.71
  },
  {
   "text": "The story goes,",
   "s": 5.385,
   "e": 6.372
  },
  {
   "text": "it happened in Syracuse,",
   "s": 6.742,
   "e": 8.07
  },
  {
   "text": "over two thousand years ago.",
   "s": 8.459,
   "e": 9.895
  },
  {
   "text": "Archimedes wrote to King Hiero:",
   "s": 10.579,
   "e": 12.261
  },
  {
   "text": "with the right machine,",
   "s": 12.911,
   "e": 13.992
  },
  {
   "text": "any weight can be moved by a small force.",
   "s": 14.404,
   "e": 16.764
  },
  {
   "text": "Give me another world to stand on,",
   "s": 17.401,
   "e": 18.923
  },
  {
   "text": "and I'll move this one.",
   "s": 19.325,
   "e": 20.17
  },
  {
   "text": "The king had a better test.",
   "s": 20.878,
   "e": 22.091
  },
  {
   "text": "He picked one of the biggest ships in his navy,",
   "s": 22.5,
   "e": 24.248
  },
  {
   "text": "with three masts,",
   "s": 24.53,
   "e": 25.417
  },
  {
   "text": "dragged up onto the beach by crowds of men.",
   "s": 25.759,
   "e": 27.697
  },
  {
   "text": "Then he filled it with cargo and passengers.",
   "s": 28.077,
   "e": 29.851
  },
  {
   "text": "Dozens of sailors couldn't budge it.",
   "s": 30.528,
   "e": 32.088
  },
  {
   "text": "And Archimedes was just one man.",
   "s": 32.572,
   "e": 34.186
  },
  {
   "text": "So he didn't use muscle.",
   "s": 34.792,
   "e": 36.961
  },
  {
   "text": "He used rope. He ran one rope around a set of wheels called pulleys,",
   "s": 37.587,
   "e": 40.483
  },
  {
   "text": "back and forth,",
   "s": 40.708,
   "e": 41.33
  },
  {
   "text": "again and again.",
   "s": 41.62,
   "e": 42.395
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the trick.",
   "s": 42.769,
   "e": 43.439
  },
  {
   "text": "Every loop of rope shares the weight.",
   "s": 43.724,
   "e": 45.516
  },
  {
   "text": "With ten loops,",
   "s": 45.739,
   "e": 46.6
  },
  {
   "text": "each one holds only a tenth.",
   "s": 46.785,
   "e": 48.24
  },
  {
   "text": "He has to pull ten times more rope,",
   "s": 48.916,
   "e": 50.683
  },
  {
   "text": "but with a tenth of the strength.",
   "s": 51.11,
   "e": 52.288
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Archimedes sat down,",
   "s": 52.993,
   "e": 54.337
  },
  {
   "text": "far away,",
   "s": 54.755,
   "e": 55.383
  },
  {
   "text": "and gently pulled.",
   "s": 55.884,
   "e": 56.721
  },
  {
   "text": "And the giant ship slid across the sand toward him,",
   "s": 57.438,
   "e": 59.985
  },
  {
   "text": "as smoothly as if it were floating. Today, every crane,",
   "s": 60.4,
   "e": 62.194
  },
  {
   "text": "elevator and tow truck uses that same idea.",
   "s": 62.883,
   "e": 66.245
  },
  {
   "text": "Trade distance for strength,",
   "s": 66.873,
   "e": 67.95
  },
  {
   "text": "and one person can move a ship.",
   "s": 68.274,
   "e": 69.624
  }
 ]
}